    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a heavy emphasis on exploiting exploitable matchups against weaker arms. **Jose Caballero** (78.35) and **Corbin Carroll** (78.18) headline our production expectations, both benefiting significantly from favorable platoon splits against Aldegheri and Kay. **Seiya Suzuki** (75.03) rounds out our elite-tier threats, receiving a nice bump from wind conditions and an advantageous matchup against Sean Sullivan. While **James Wood** (70.07) is facing a more competent arm in Avila, his elite 0.407 xwOBA and lead-off spot make him an essential anchor for our stolen base pursuit. We are prioritizing these high-efficiency scorers to buffer our 5x5 categories, specifically leveraging the mobility of our outfielders to stay competitive in the SB department.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal range at the bottom of our infield. **Alex Freeland** (41.24) ultimately hit the pine, falling just short of the 40-point efficiency floor necessary to justify a start given his lower-order placement in the lineup against McClanahan. The optimizer opted for the higher upside of **Max Muncy** (46.74), banking on his park factor advantage despite the difficult matchup against Ashcraft. We are closely monitoring the status of **Josh Naylor**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Max Muncy**, **Brice Turang**, **Kyle Karros**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Cole Young**, as the current \"Lineup Pending\" status introduces variance into our projected efficiency. Should these lineups finalize with these players hitting lower than anticipated, we may see further adjustments to our expected outputs. Note that **Mickey Moniak** remains on the IL, further tightening our flexible bench options.",
